.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt GFXTOOL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gfxtool
.Nd inspect the firmware display on an unbound Intel HD 4400
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm dump
.Nm
.Cm crc
.Ar A|B|C frames
.Nm
.Cm capture
.Ar A|B|C file.ppm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
uses
.Pa /dev/mem
to inspect the Intel Haswell HD 4400 at PCI function 0000:00:02.0.
It refuses any identity but 8086:0a16, disabled memory decoding, BARs
above 4 GiB and an aperture other than 256 MiB.
It checks the PCI driver link, uevent and DRM device identities.
A GPU that a driver owns, or whose ownership check cannot complete, is
refused by
.Cm crc ;
.Cm dump
and
.Cm capture
read it through a read-only mapping, write no register, and say so on
standard error.
Run it as root.
.Pp
.Cm dump
prints named display, panel power, PWM, power-well, forcewake, GT FIFO,
status-page and interrupt registers, among them
.Dv GEN7_ERR_INT ,
whose low bits latch the pipes' FIFO underruns, the render, video,
blitter and video-enhancement rings, and all 65536 GGTT entries of the
CPU-visible aperture.
On an unbound GPU, ring reads temporarily request forcewake; a prior
request is preserved.
On an owned GPU they read the GT as its driver left it.
.Pp
.Cm crc
enables the selected pipe's post-panel-fitter CRC source, skips the
first two frames, and prints the frame counter and five hexadecimal
CRC words for each requested frame.
The frame count is 1 through 1000000.
It requires an enabled primary plane and refuses an already enabled CRC.
A frame that changes during the read fails the command.
The saved CRC control is restored on exit.
The command preserves firmware routing; a Haswell eDP route that bypasses
the panel fitter needs a mode set before this CRC source can be used.
.Pp
.Cm capture
reads the primary plane's surface, source offset, stride and source size
and writes a binary PPM of its pixels through the GGTT aperture.
It supports linear RGB565, XRGB8888, XBGR8888, XRGB2101010 and
XBGR2101010, converting each to eight bits per colour.
It refuses disabled, tiled, rotated and unknown formats and a surface
outside the aperture.
It captures the primary plane before gamma, scaling and cursor composition.
It refuses an existing output file and removes a partial capture on failure.
.Pp
Each register wait ends after at most one second or 10000 reads.
Interrupt, termination, hangup and broken-pipe signals return through
cleanup, which restores temporary register changes.
Forced termination cannot run cleanup.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 1 on refusal or an I/O failure, and 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mem 4 ,
.Xr watchdog 4
